Subject: [PATCH 4/7] media: qcom: camss: video: expose the sensor stream's controls

Applications that drive a camera through its video nodes need the controls
there, as the Tegra VI provides them. Each video node gets a control
handler that inherits the controls of the sensor stream the node captures:
for a sensor with the streams API, those of the subdev feeding the sink pad
the stream is routed from; otherwise the sensor's own.

The media graph can change between uses, so the handler is rebuilt when the
node is opened and no other handle is open on it.
---
--- a/camss-csid.c
+++ b/camss-csid.c
@@ -902,6 +902,32 @@ unlock:
 }
 
 /*
+ * msm_csid_pad_stream - The sensor stream a CSID source pad carries
+ * @sd: CSID V4L2 subdevice
+ * @pad: Source pad
+ *
+ * Return the stream the pad is capturing, or is set to capture when it starts
+ */
+u32 msm_csid_pad_stream(struct v4l2_subdev *sd, unsigned int pad)
+{
+	struct csid_device *csid = v4l2_get_subdevdata(sd);
+	u8 rdi = pad - MSM_CSID_PAD_FIRST_SRC;
+	u32 stream;
+
+	if (pad < MSM_CSID_PAD_FIRST_SRC || pad >= MSM_CSID_PADS_NUM)
+		return 0;
+
+	mutex_lock(&csid->stream_lock);
+	if (csid->streaming & BIT(rdi))
+		stream = csid->route[rdi].stream;
+	else
+		stream = v4l2_ctrl_g_ctrl(csid->rdi_stream[rdi]);
+	mutex_unlock(&csid->stream_lock);
+
+	return stream;
+}
+
